<Layout title="About Cosmin Ghinoiu — Implementation & Delivery" description="My background spans technical support, client engagement and enterprise implementation. I bring practical structure, cross-functional coordination and follow-through to delivery." current="/about/">
  <section class="about-intro section-wrap"><div><h1>I’m Cosmin. <br />I make delivery <br />workable.</h1><a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/cosmin-ghinoiu/" rel="me">Connect on LinkedIn <Arrow direction="up-right" /></a></div><div class="about-opening"><p>I do my best work when delivery is complicated: technical dependencies, competing priorities, and different teams looking at the same problem from different angles.</p><p>My role is to work out what needs to happen, turn it into a practical plan, and keep the right people moving in the same direction.</p><p>I now offer that experience through independent implementation and rollout work, on a defined project or embedded with your team.</p></div></section>
  <section class="about-background section-wrap"><h2>Experience across <br />the whole handover.</h2><div class="prose"><p>My background spans technical support, client engagement and enterprise implementation. That combination helps me connect the details of how software works with the needs of the people introducing, using and supporting it.</p><p>Between 2022 and July 2026, I led more than 50 specialized delivery projects, including implementations, integrations, migrations, technical reviews and workflow redesigns. Much of that work involved global pharmaceutical and life-sciences organizations.</p><p>I have also delivered more than 100 live user and administrator training sessions. Enablement has been part of the delivery work throughout, from explaining a configuration to helping a team prepare for operational ownership.</p><a class="text-link" href="/selected-work/">See the project examples <Arrow /></a></div></section>
  <section class="working-style section-wrap" id="working-practices"><div class="section-heading"><h2>How I work.</h2><p>Enough structure to help people execute. <br class="desktop-break" /> Clear decisions. Practical follow-through.</p></div><div class="working-rows"><article><h3>Start with the real work</h3><p>I work through the requirements, constraints and current workflows before settling on a delivery approach. The plan needs to fit the situation.</p></article><article><h3>Make ownership visible</h3><p>I connect business needs with technical reality, bring the right people into decisions, and keep actions and dependencies clear.</p></article><article><h3>Leave useful knowledge behind</h3><p>During employment, I led a weekly peer knowledge-sharing program over one year and helped develop reusable delivery and review frameworks. I bring the same attention to training, documentation and handover.</p></article></div></section>
  <ContactClose />
</Layout>
